x-systemd.requires so the loop devices, VG activation, and mount are fully reconstructed at boot. Restarted node1 twice via `systemctl reboot`: the first reboot exposed a systemd ordering cycle (fixed by removing local-fs.target Requires/dependency loop and switching to DefaultDependencies=no/Before=local-fs.target), and the second reboot verified the fix — boot ID changed, and /srv/data came back mounted at 2.5G with matching data checksum and no failed units, with no manual intervention.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 disk layout and found no free space on the sole disk (vda)\",\"Installed lvm2 package via dnf\",\"Created two loopback-backed files (1G, 1.5G) as PVs since no spare partition existed\",\"Created VG data_vg, LV data_lv, xfs filesystem, mounted at /srv/data, wrote test file\",\"Extended VG with second loop device, grew LV to 2.49G and xfs_growfs while mounted, verified data intact\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, lvs/vgs, df, md5sum of test file\",\"Created and enabled systemd unit to reattach loop devices and activate VG at boot; added matching /etc/fstab entry\",\"Rebooted node1 via systemd-run scheduled systemctl reboot; polled until reachable again\",\"Found and fixed a systemd ordering cycle preventing boot-time activation (removed conflicting local-fs.target Requires, switched to DefaultDependencies=no)\",\"Manually verified recovery after first reboot, then rebooted node1 a second time to prove the fix works unattended at real boot time\",\"Verified post-second-reboot: LV active, VG has both PVs, /srv/data mounted at 2.5G, test file content and md5sum unchanged, no failed systemd units\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"LV created and mounted at /srv/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cffbfd4667944780\"],\"summary\":\"pvcreate/vgcreate/lvcreate/mkfs.xfs/mount produced /srv/data on data_vg/data_lv (~956M) with a test file written\"},{\"requirement\":\"LV grown to at least 2GB while mounted, contents intact\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-67ac7af371044f88\"],\"summary\":\"vgextend+lvextend+xfs_growfs resized to 2.49G live; mount stayed active throughout and testfile.txt content was re-read successfully afterward\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98374d8e611f4e26\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 67f3a44b..., uptime, lvs/vgs showing 2 PVs healthy, df 2.5G mount, md5sum of test file, and enabled persistence service\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-69f8fe645d0f4c79\"],\"summary\":\"systemd-run scheduled systemctl reboot and returned immediately with the timer/service unit names\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving restart (1st reboot)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d1bec72741cb46b7\",\"cmd-257a3cf59a624d51\",\"cmd-2bffc2fb933d42f2\",\"cmd-28698cf853c1442d\"],\"summary\":\"Polled boot_id (still 67f3a44b...), then connection timed out during reboot, then new boot_id 47ea332d... with fresh uptime confirmed restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Diagnosed and fixed boot-time recovery failure after 1st reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5e25c632e6cc43a9\",\"cmd-4118c76e4b704064\",\"cmd-ef7e8c7177af4c81\",\"cmd-68dbb730ce5a4106\"],\"summary\":\"First reboot showed VG/mount missing due to a systemd ordering cycle; fixed unit dependencies, manually reactivated and confirmed data intact, then verified no ordering cycle/failed units remained\"},{\"requirement\":\"Second restart used to prove unattended boot-time recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f5425d63eba44305\",\"cmd-b363ddc1752c4b7f\",\"cmd-2012e80c47b04086\",\"cmd-d4a1cc52bdce42bb\"],\"summary\":\"Scheduled second reboot, polled through disconnection, observed new boot_id 52e383fa... with fresh uptime confirming a genuine second restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery: LV, mount, data, cluster/service health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-729e75cd22d44145\"],\"summary\":\"After the fixed second reboot, /srv/data auto-mounted at 2.5G, data_vg showed both PVs active, test file md5sum matched baseline exactly, persistence service active, and no failed systemd units\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, built an LVM logical volume (data_vg/data_lv) mounted at /srv/data using two loop-backed PVs (root disk had no spare partition), initially sized ~956M, then grew it live to 2.49G via vgextend+lvextend+xfs_growfs while it stayed mounted and its test file remained intact. Set up a systemd oneshot unit (data-lv-loop-setup.service) plus an fstab entry with x-systemd.requires so the loop devices, VG activation, and mount are fully reconstructed at boot. Restarted node1 twice via `systemctl reboot`: the first reboot exposed a systemd ordering cycle (fixed by removing local-fs.target Requires/dependency loop and switching to DefaultDependencies=no/Before=local-fs.target), and the second reboot verified the fix — boot ID changed, and /srv/data came back mounted at 2.5G with matching data checksum and no failed units, with no manual intervention.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 disk layout and found no free space on the sole disk (vda)","Installed lvm2 package via dnf","Created two loopback-backed files (1G, 1.5G) as PVs since no spare partition existed","Created VG data_vg, LV data_lv, xfs filesystem, mounted at /srv/data, wrote test file","Extended VG with second loop device, grew LV to 2.49G and xfs_growfs while mounted, verified data intact","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, lvs/vgs, df, md5sum of test file","Created and enabled systemd unit to reattach loop devices and activate VG at boot; added matching /etc/fstab entry","Rebooted node1 via systemd-run scheduled systemctl reboot; polled until reachable again","Found and fixed a systemd ordering cycle preventing boot-time activation (removed conflicting local-fs.target Requires, switched to DefaultDependencies=no)","Manually verified recovery after first reboot, then rebooted node1 a second time to prove the fix works unattended at real boot time","Verified post-second-reboot: LV active, VG has both PVs, /srv/data mounted at 2.5G, test file content and md5sum unchanged, no failed systemd units"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"LV created and mounted at /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-cffbfd4667944780"],"summary":"pvcreate/vgcreate/lvcreate/mkfs.xfs/mount produced /srv/data on data_vg/data_lv (~956M) with a test file written"},{"requirement":"LV grown to at least 2GB while mounted, contents intact","command_ids":["cmd-67ac7af371044f88"],"summary":"vgextend+lvextend+xfs_growfs resized to 2.49G live; mount stayed active throughout and testfile.txt content was re-read successfully afterward"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart","command_ids":["cmd-98374d8e611f4e26"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 67f3a44b..., uptime, lvs/vgs showing 2 PVs healthy, df 2.5G mount, md5sum of test file, and enabled persistence service"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-69f8fe645d0f4c79"],"summary":"systemd-run scheduled systemctl reboot and returned immediately with the timer/service unit names"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving restart (1st reboot)","command_ids":["cmd-d1bec72741cb46b7","cmd-257a3cf59a624d51","cmd-2bffc2fb933d42f2","cmd-28698cf853c1442d"],"summary":"Polled boot_id (still 67f3a44b...), then connection timed out during reboot, then new boot_id 47ea332d... with fresh uptime confirmed restart"},{"requirement":"Diagnosed and fixed boot-time recovery failure after 1st reboot","command_ids":["cmd-5e25c632e6cc43a9","cmd-4118c76e4b704064","cmd-ef7e8c7177af4c81","cmd-68dbb730ce5a4106"],"summary":"First reboot showed VG/mount missing due to a systemd ordering cycle; fixed unit dependencies, manually reactivated and confirmed data intact, then verified no ordering cycle/failed units remained"},{"requirement":"Second restart used to prove unattended boot-time recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f